1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 e6 3. c4 b6 4. Nc3 Bb7 5. d5 Bb4 6. Bg5 h6 7. Bxf6 Qxf6 8. Rc1
O-O 9. e4 exd5 10. exd5 Na6 11. Be2 Rfe8 12. O-O Bxc3 13. Rxc3 Nc5 14. Nd4 d6
15. Rf3 Qe5 16. Re1 a5 17. Rxf7 Kxf7 18. Bh5+ g6 19. Rxe5 Rxe5 20. Bg4 Bc8 21.
h3 Bxg4 22. Qxg4 Rae8 23. f3 h5 24. Qf4+ Kg7 25. Qd2 Re1+ 26. Kh2 Ra1 27. Qc3
Kf7 28. b4 Ree1 29. bxc5 h4 30. Qxe1 Rxe1 31. c6 Ke7 32. g4 Rc1 33. Ne6 Rxc4
34. Nxc7 {(Tinsley now gives the finish as 34...RxP 35.P-B4 R-QKt7 36.P-B5 PxP
37.PxP P-R5 Resigns, but he appears to have missed out two half-moves - JS)}
Rc2+ 35. Kg1 Rxa2 36. f4 Rb2 37. f5 gxf5 38. gxf5 a4 {Sources: Tinsley
notebooks; Manchester Guardian, 13 Aug 1924; The Scotsman, 14 Aug 1924, p3.
Fairhurst, at 21, was cited as the youngest player ever to play in the British
Championship (Western Daily Press - Tuesday 12 August 1924)} 0-1

