{(Tinsley notebook gives 14...Q-Q2 but this must be 14...Q-Q3 as otherwise
Black's move 16 would leave a knight en prise - JS)} 15. Bb3 O-O-O 16. c4 Nf4
17. Qe3 Ng6 18. Bd2 Ng4 19. Qe4 Bf6 20. c5 Qc7 {(Another indicator that 14...
Qd6 was played - had the Q been on d7, there would have been no need for this
move - JS)} 21. Bxe6+ fxe6 22. Qxg6 Bxd4 23. Qxe6+ Kb8 24. g3 Bxf2+ 25. Kg2
Rhf8 26. Red1 Bxc5 27. Bf4 Rxf4 28. Rxd8+ Qxd8 29. gxf4 Qd3 30. Re1 Ne3+ 31.
Kh1 Ng4 32. Qe2 Qd5 33. h3 Ne3 34. Rg1 Qf5 {(34...Q-B5 written but must be as
per text - JS)} 35. Rg5 Qxh3+ 36. Nh2 Bd4 37. Rxh5 Qe6 38. Qd3 Qxa2 39. Rg5
Qxb2 40. Nf3 Qf2 41. Nxd4 {Source: Tinsley notebooks (in the margin at the end
is written "S. 4 Ps to 1 [illegible] down")} 1/2-1/2

