1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Bxc6 dxc6 5. Nc3 Bd6 6. d4 f6 {An
extraordinary blunder.} 7. dxe5 fxe5 8. Nxe5 Qf6 9. Nd3 Qg6 10. O-O Bg4 11. f3
Bd7 12. Bf4 O-O-O 13. Qe1 Bxf4 14. Nxf4 Qf7 15. Qe3 b6 16. Rfd1 Ne7 $1 17. a4 {
White embarks on a combination which is not quite sound.} a5 18. b4 axb4 19. a5
$1 Kb7 20. axb6 cxb6 21. Qe2 Bc8 $3 {The only defence. If 21 ...b5 then 22
Nxb5 axb5 23 Rxd7+ Rxd7 24 Qxb5+ & wins.} 22. Qa6+ Kc7 23. Qa7+ Bb7 24. Nce2
Qc4 25. Qa4 g5 26. Nd3 c5 27. Qb3 Qxb3 28. cxb3 {Black has the better ending.}
Nc6 29. Kf2 Na5 30. Rab1 Ba6 31. Ke3 Rhe8 32. Nf2 Bc4 33. Rxd8 Rxd8 34. Nc1 Be6
35. Nfd3 Nc6 36. g3 Nd4 37. f4 gxf4+ 38. gxf4 Nc2+ 39. Kd2 Na3 40. Ra1 Rg8 41.
Ne1 Rg1 42. f5 Bd7 {"B-K2" Tinsley} 43. Ra2 Rh1 44. Kd1 Nb5 45. Kd2 Rxh2+ {
and Black won on the 75th move. (To here, notes by Fairhurst. Thanks to the
Tinsley notebooks we have the moves...)} 46. Ke3 Rxa2 47. Nxa2 Kd6 48. Kf4 Nd4
49. Nc1 Ke7 {"K-Q2"} 50. Ng2 Be8 51. e5 c4 52. bxc4 b3 53. Nd3 Nxf5 54. Nb2 Bg6
55. Ne1 Nd4 56. Ng2 Nc2 57. Nh4 Ke6 58. Nf3 h6 {"P-QR3"} 59. Nd2 Nd4 60. Nf1
Nc6 61. Nd2 Bc2 62. Nf3 h5 63. Na4 {"Kt-R4" ambiguous} Bg6 64. Kg5 Be8 {
"B-Qsq" (Tinsley's notation can be quite terrible!)} 65. Nb2 Na5 66. Nd3 Nxc4
67. Nd4+ Kd5 68. Nxb3 Nxe5 69. Nf4+ Kc4 70. Nd2+ Kc3 71. Ne4+ Kd4 72. Nd6 Nf7+
73. Nxf7 Bxf7 74. Kf6 Ke3 {Source: (moves 1-45) Chess Scotland archive (thanks
to Alan McGowan); (moves 45-74) Tinsley notebooks} 0-1

