{"Arbroathian's Success in Chess Tournament.—At the annual congress of the
British Chess Federation held at Southport from 11th to 23rd August, Mr H. A.
Turriff, 36 Victoria Street, Arbroath, won first prize in Section A of the
Second class tournament, with a possible of nine successive wins. Before
coming to Arbroath, Mr Turriff was for three years in succession champion of
the Aberdeen Chess Club, besides winning numerous other firsts. In 1908 he won
the Minor Championship of the Scottish Chess Association at Dundee. He is
well-known in Scottish chess circles as a keen student and practitioner of the
game, playing one of the top boards in the Dundee Chess Club’s Richardson
Cup team. The following was the first game finished at the Southport Congress:
-"} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. c3 Nf6 4. d4 Nxe4 5. d5 Ne7 6. Nxe5 d6 7. Bb5+ c6 8.
dxc6 bxc6 9. Nxc6 Qb6 10. Nd4+ Kd8 11. O-O Bb7 12. Be3 Kc7 13. Ne6+ {Source:
Arbroath Herald and Advertiser, 29 Aug 1924. For more on this player see http:/
/www.chessscotland.com/history/biographies/turriff.htm (n.b. FO Nelson was
from York)} 1-0

